body-scanner-tab-report = Patient condition
body-scanner-tab-plan = Operation plan
body-scanner-plan-description = Recommendations based on the current patient. Resolved problems disappear automatically. This is not a list of available operations: access, tools and restrictions are checked in the surgery panel.
body-scanner-plan-empty = No surgical tasks detected by the scan.
body-scanner-plan-prepare = Preparation. Stabilize the patient before intervention. Prepare sterile instruments, medical gloves and a mask; disinfect the relevant area with ethanol. Apply a clean disposable sterile drape if needed.
body-scanner-plan-debride = { $part }: remove necrotic tissue. Open this area if necessary. Tools: scalpel → hemostat → saline (10 units). Antibiotics do not remove necrosis.
body-scanner-plan-heart = { $part }: reconstruct the damaged heart through the ribcage. Tools: scalpel → hemostat → hemostat. A dead heart cannot be restored.
body-scanner-plan-organ-necrosis = { $part }: organ necrosis. Open the appropriate area and debride: scalpel → hemostat → saline (10 units).
body-scanner-plan-dead-organ = { $part }: dead organ. Prepare a compatible viable donor organ, remove the dead organ and transplant the replacement. Dead organs cannot be reimplanted.
body-scanner-plan-replace-organ = { $part }: organ necrosis; a repair operation is unavailable for this condition. Prepare a compatible viable donor organ and replace the damaged organ.
body-scanner-plan-dead-limb = { $part }: dead tissue. Prepare a compatible limb or prosthesis, remove the dead part and attach the replacement. Dead parts cannot be restored.
body-scanner-plan-missing-organ = { $part }: missing organ. Prepare a clean compatible donor and implant it through the appropriate area. Consult the implantation operation for steps and tools.
body-scanner-plan-missing-part = { $part }: missing body part. Prepare a clean compatible replacement. Restore any missing parent part first: arm before hand, leg before foot.
body-scanner-plan-glass = { $part }: remove embedded glass using the fragment extraction operation and a hemostat. Recheck until no fragments remain.
body-scanner-plan-infection = { $part }: treat infection with surgicillin and monitor progress. An open infected wound can be irrigated with saline (10 units). Irrigation complements treatment; antibiotics do not remove contamination or necrosis.
body-scanner-plan-slime-infection = { $part }: slime tissue purity compromised. Monitor the tissue; irrigate an open infected area with saline (10 units).
body-scanner-plan-clean = { $part }: disinfect the contaminated area with ethanol before closure. Saline is used for infected wound irrigation. Use pure solutions; specialized surgical bottles avoid the container sterility penalty.
body-scanner-plan-observe = { $part }: residual contamination in a closed area. Monitor incubation and infection; contamination gradually decreases while closed. This alone does not require another incision.
body-scanner-plan-organ-infection = { $part }: contamination or infection inside the organ. Monitor for necrosis; treating infection does not replace surgical treatment of dying tissue.
body-scanner-plan-close = { $part }: after necessary interventions, complete the closure operation for this area using the tools listed in its steps. Close other open areas separately.
body-scanner-plan-undrape = { $part }: remove the disposable sterile drape when finished; do not reuse it.
body-scanner-plan-recheck = Follow-up. Recheck bleeding, open areas, organ condition and infection in the Patient condition tab.
